            },
            "body": "> The helper makes sense and the test covers the merge. One gap: only the `xgrammar` branch calls `grammar_stop_token_ids`. `llguidance` still receives the raw `eos_token_ids`, and so do custom backends from `GRAMMAR_BACKEND_REGISTRY`, so the same early-stop on `tokenizer.eos_token_id` or `additional_stop_token_ids` can still happen there. Worth computing the list once at the top of `create_grammar_backend` and passing it to every branch?\r\n\r\nGood catch, thanks. create_grammar_backend now merges the stop ids once at the top and passes them to every backend, including registry backends and llguidance. Added a test that a registered backend receives the tokenizer's stop tokens.",
